[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi!</p>\n<p>I was trying to use <code>Function.bicompl</code> with <code>Iff.intro</code> but I ran into some universe issues (I think).<br>\nI kinda tracked it down to the fact that the type variables in <code>bicompl</code> are declared as <code>Type*</code> instead of <code>Sort*</code> and I wonder why that is the case. Doesn't that just limit the possible applications of e.g. <code>bicompl</code>? (Is my understanding even correct?)</p>\n<p>More concretely, I was basically trying to do the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583882342,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775516555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does anything in mathlib break if you change it to Sort* in Function.bicompl?</p>",
        "id": 583882447,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1775516621
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It could be just an oversight</p>",
        "id": 583882568,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1775516706
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Uhh I haven't tried that yet <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span> I don't understand (yet) how I would change the Mathlib code and check if anything breaks</p>",
        "id": 583882635,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775516746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I will read up on how to test Mathlib after making the required changes.</p>",
        "id": 583882936,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775516958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In general though, would there be any reason why Type* would be preferred over Sort*?</p>",
        "id": 583882960,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775516979
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>instead of <code>Function.bicompl</code> I think it's preferred to just write a lambda</p>",
        "id": 583883105,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1775517073
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I know, I just wanted to experiment a bit.</p>",
        "id": 583883138,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775517095
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright. I made the following change and everything seems to work fine.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Changing all variables to Sort* did not work. For example, it led to the <code>uncurry_bicompr</code> theorem breaking.</p>",
        "id": 583883808,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775517593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Should I open a PR?</p>",
        "id": 583884159,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775517855
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hm. Changing only ε to Sort* keeps everything in Mathlib working, but it doesn't suffice for my use case. The following does however:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Compose a binary function `f` with a pair of unary functions `g` and `h`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">If both arguments of `f` have the same type and `g = h`, then `bicompl f g g = f on g`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, changing all variables to Sort* breaks the usage of <code>Prod.map</code> in the <code>uncurry_bicompl</code> theorem (as well as breaking the <code>uncurry_bicompr</code> theorem).<br>\nThis leads me to a further question: why would <code>Prod.map</code> also only use Type*??</p>",
        "id": 583885595,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775518937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Because <code>Prod</code> uses <code>Type*</code>, as opposed to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=PProd#doc\">docs#PProd</a></p>",
        "id": 583886075,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775519363
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hm. Thank you. I don't quite understand now if this should affect the Bicomp section or if the uncurry_bicomp{l,r} theorems should be changed to just work with (other variables of) Type* instead.<br>\nThis would be the most general solution I think. It would allow for using bicompl with Props.</p>",
        "id": 583886269,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775519534
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bicomp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Compose a binary function `f` with a pair of unary functions `g` and `h`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">If both arguments of `f` have the same type and `g = h`, then `bicompl f g g = f on g`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Compose a unary function `f` with a binary function `g`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bicompr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Suggested local notation:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">notation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" ∘₂ \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bicompr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry_bicompr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry_bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bicompl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bicomp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Like this. (Ignore my code example with the <code>#check</code>)</p>",
        "id": 583886344,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1775519623
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We're also missing <code>f.bicompl g g = f.onFun g</code> even though it appears in the docstring of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Function.bicompl#doc\">docs#Function.bicompl</a></p>",
        "id": 583889044,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775520597
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Summing.20over.20a.20.60Prop.60\">#new members &gt; Summing over a &#96;Prop&#96;</a> might be relevant to the topic title</p>",
